\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Loss increases in nats per target, relative to intact history, on 69,376 identical targets. Neural values are mean $\pm $ sample standard deviation over three seeds. $G_k$ retains the nearest $k$ tokens; shuffling preserves the nearest 128 and permutes only earlier tokens. KenLM invariance holds per target, not merely in the aggregate.}}{11}{table.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:interventions}{{6}{11}{Loss increases in nats per target, relative to intact history, on 69,376 identical targets. Neural values are mean $\pm $ sample standard deviation over three seeds. $G_k$ retains the nearest $k$ tokens; shuffling preserves the nearest 128 and permutes only earlier tokens. KenLM invariance holds per target, not merely in the aggregate}{table.6}{}}
